# Trivy ignore list for the CareLink services (read by ci.yaml and cd.yaml).
#
# Rules for this file:
#   - An ID goes here only when no fixed version exists on the version line we
#     run. Each group says why, and whether our code can reach the flaw.
#   - Every entry has an exp: date. After it, Trivy stops ignoring the ID and
#     the pipeline fails again, which forces a fresh review.
#   - The scans run with --show-suppressed, so the CI log lists every entry
#     that still matches. Delete an entry as soon as it stops showing there.
#
# Why these remain: the services run Spring Boot 2.7.18, Spring Framework
# 5.3.39 and Spring Cloud 2021.0.9, the last open-source releases of those
# lines. Fixes for the IDs below ship only in Spring Boot 3 / Framework 6
# (javax -> jakarta migration) or in paid extended support. Moving to Boot 3
# is the real fix and is planned as its own piece of work.
#
# Last reviewed 22 Nov 2026 against CI on PR #29: 31 entries (5 CRITICAL,
# 26 HIGH). The patch upgrade in that PR fixed 69 of the original 100.

# ---- Spring Framework 5.3.39 -------------------------------------------------
# CRITICAL, spring-web: Java deserialization in HttpInvoker remoting.
# Not reachable: no service uses HttpInvoker or any Spring remoting exporter.
CVE-2016-1000027 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-webflux: path traversal when functional routes
# (RouterFunctions.resources) serve static files. Not reachable: the gateway
# serves its frontend through the default static handler, and no service
# defines RouterFunctions.resources.
CVE-2024-38816 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2024-38819 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-core: annotation detection on generic super types, which matters
# for method security. Not reachable: no @PreAuthorize/@Secured anywhere.
CVE-2025-41249 exp:2026-12-31
# CRITICAL and HIGH, spring-webmvc, spring-webflux and spring-expression:
# no open-source 5.3 release fixes these.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-41842 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-41845 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-41849 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-41850 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- Spring Security 5.7.11 (managed by Boot 2.7.18) -------------------------
# CRITICAL, spring-security-web: authorization bypass for WebFlux static
# resources. Not reachable today: the gateway has no authorization rules to
# bypass (anyExchange().permitAll() in InsecurityConfiguration). That is a gap
# of its own (the app has no login), not a reason to keep this forever.
CVE-2024-38821 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-22732 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-security-core: AuthenticatedVoter with a null Authentication.
# Not reachable: AuthenticatedVoter is not used.
CVE-2024-22257 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-security-crypto: BCrypt ignores input past 72 bytes.
# Not reachable: no service hashes passwords (no PasswordEncoder).
CVE-2025-22228 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- Spring Boot 2.7.18 ------------------------------------------------------
# HIGH, spring-boot: EndpointRequest.to() matcher is wrong for unexposed
# endpoints. Not reachable: EndpointRequest is not used.
CVE-2025-22235 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-boot and spring-boot-starter-actuator: no 2.7 fix. Reduced
# exposure: actuator listens only on the private management port 8090, which
# the ALB cannot reach; the gateway forwards just /actuator/health to it.
CVE-2026-40973 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-22733 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- Spring Cloud 2021.0.9 (Gateway 3.1.9, Sleuth) ---------------------------
# HIGH, spring-cloud-gateway-server: X-Forwarded-* / Forwarded headers from
# untrusted clients are passed on. Not used for decisions: no service reads
# those headers or the remote address.
CVE-2025-41235 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-cloud-gateway-server: SpEL in route definitions can read
# environment variables. Needs an attacker who can change routes; ours come
# only from our own Helm ConfigMap, and the gateway actuator endpoint is on
# the private management port.
CVE-2025-41253 exp:2026-12-31
# HIGH, spring-cloud-sleuth-instrumentation: no 2021.0 fix (Sleuth is replaced
# by Micrometer Tracing in Boot 3).
CVE-2026-41708 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- Spring Data 2021.2 and Micrometer 1.9 (managed by Boot 2.7.18) ----------
# HIGH, spring-data-commons and micrometer-core: no fix on these lines.
CVE-2026-41716 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-40984 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- Jackson 2.13.5 (managed by Boot 2.7.18) ---------------------------------
# HIGH, jackson-core and jackson-databind. CVE-2025-52999 is a stack overflow
# on deeply nested JSON (fixed in 2.15). Forcing a newer Jackson than Boot 2.7
# manages is untested here, so these wait for Boot 3 (Jackson 2.15+).
CVE-2025-52999 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-68494 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-89425 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-54512 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-54513 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-91776 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-91777 exp:2026-12-31

# ---- SnakeYAML 1.30 ----------------------------------------------------------
# HIGH: CVE-2022-1471 is code execution when parsing untrusted YAML with the
# default Constructor; CVE-2022-25857 is a denial of service on deep nesting.
# Must stay on 1.x: the Kubernetes Java client used by Spring Cloud Kubernetes
# calls the SafeConstructor() that SnakeYAML 2.x removed (tested on this PR:
# the gateway failed with NoSuchMethodError). We only parse our own YAML
# (application config and our own ConfigMaps), never user input.
CVE-2022-1471 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2022-25857 exp:2026-12-31
